gZx(){return"Guitar amp: drive pedal, amp tone stack and speaker cabinet"},
ga4z(){return"Riff, the modelled guitar"},
ga4y(){return"Riff is an electric guitar modelled string by string. It has no keys: cable a keyboard's MIDI OUT into its MIDI IN, or play it from a controller on its MIDI channel.\nClose notes go to separate strings, so they ring together. With Legato on, a note close to the previous one hammers on or pulls off on the same string. Overlap does the same only when you press a key before letting go of the last one.\nThe pitch wheel bends, the mod wheel adds vibrato, the sustain pedal lets strings ring. Feedback makes held strings bloom into a harmonic, like in front of an amp.\nPalm mute, Pick position, Tone and the pickup selector change strings that are already ringing: map them to a pedal or a knob with Learn and play them like a guitarist's hands. For crunch and distortion, cable Riff into the Amp."},
ga2Z(){return"Amp and cabinet IRs"},
ga2W(){return"The Amp has three sections you can switch on and off, by hand or with a footswitch: a Drive pedal (Overdrive or Distortion), the amp itself (Gain, Bass, Middle, Treble) and the speaker cabinet.\nThe cabinet shapes most of a guitar sound. Besides the three built-in ones, the Amp can play an impulse response (IR), a recording of a real cabinet: tap Load IR under the Amp and pick a .wav file. It is saved in your project; the cross next to its name removes it."},
ga2Y(){return"Where to find free cabinet IRs"},
ga2X(){return"Each pack comes with its own licence: free to play through, but usually not to share. Download them yourself from these sites."},
ga35(){return"TONE3000: a community library with thousands of free IRs"},
ga34(){return"Kalthallen Cabs: free and paid packs of classic cabinets"},
ga33(){return"Celestion: a free IR from the speaker maker"},
gZC(){return"Snaps your voice onto the notes of a scale, from subtle to robot"},
