garg(){return"Drum Pattern Format (.gfdrum)"},
garf(){return"A .gfdrum file is a YAML text file describing a drum pattern.\n\nStep grid notation:\nX = strong hit (~100)\nx = medium hit (~75)\no = soft hit (~55)\ng = ghost note (~28)\n. = rest\nSpaces and | in a grid are ignored. A grid can span two bars; grid: triplet splits each beat in three.\n\nSwing: feel (straight, swing_light, swing_hard) and swing_unit (8 = eighths, 16 = sixteenths)\nKit: kit (standard, room, power, electronic, tr808, jazz, brush, orchestra)\nVelocity fields: base_velocity, velocity_range\nTiming fields: timing_jitter, rush (in beats; negative plays ahead of the beat)\nSections: groove, fill, break, crash, intro, ending\nSection types: loop (one variation per phrase), sequence (bars in order)\nGroove variations can have a role (intro, verse, chorus, bridge) for the song form.\n\nThe full format is described on the website, under .gfdrum."},
