gazb(){return"Calibrate"},
gaze(){return"Measure this device"},
gazc(){return"Your device takes a moment to play sound, and another to capture it. Together that delay would put every take behind the beat, so it is measured once and subtracted from what you record.\n\nThe measurement plays a few short sweeps and listens for them coming back through the microphone \u2014 so it has to be able to hear them:\n\n\u2022  Use the speaker, not headphones. On headphones the microphone hears nothing and the measurement fails.\n\u2022  Turn the volume up.\n\u2022  Keep the room quiet for the few seconds it takes.\n\nMeasure again after switching to a Bluetooth speaker or headset: the delay belongs to the gear, not to the tune, and Bluetooth adds a great deal of it."},
