ga4L(){return"Start here"},
gOm(){return"Modules"},
ga4F(){return"How sound moves between modules"},
ga4E(){return"Tap the cable icon at the top of the rack to see the back of your modules. That is where you connect them with cables."},
ga4D(){return"An instrument plays through the speakers on its own. You do not need a cable to hear it."},
ga4A(){return"Yellow cables carry notes (MIDI), from a keyboard to an instrument. Red and white cables carry sound, left and right."},
ga4C(){return"To put an effect after an instrument, cable the instrument's AUDIO OUT L and R into the effect's AUDIO IN L and R. What comes out of the effect goes to the speakers."},
ga4B(){return"To draw a cable, long-press a socket and drag it to another one. Sockets that accept it light up while you drag."},
gOn(){return"Watch the clip"},
ga4l(){return"Play in a scale"},
ga4k(){return"Every new project has a keyboard and a Xen module.\nHold a key and tap a scale, for example Blues. Xen switches on, and the key you hold becomes the root note.\nOpen Family for other traditions: maqamat, ragas, Japanese scales and more."},
ga4j(){return"Grey keys are outside the scale: press one and you hear the nearest note that fits."},
ga43(){return"Add an effect to your keyboard"},
ga42(){return"Tap + and pick an effect, for example Reverb.\nTap the cable icon at the top.\nLong-press the keyboard's red AUDIO OUT L and drag it to the effect's AUDIO IN L. Then the white R to R.\nTap the back arrow and play."},
ga41(){return"You hear the keyboard through the effect. Turn its knobs to change the sound."},
ga4i(){return"Remove a cable or a module"},
ga4h(){return"A cable: in the cable view, tap the small \u2715 in the middle of the cable, then Disconnect.\nA module: tap the bin icon at the top of the module, then Remove. Its cables go with it."},
ga4g(){return""},
ga46(){return"Play the guitar from the keyboard"},
ga45(){return"Tap + and pick Riff.\nIn the cable view, drag the keyboard's yellow MIDI OUT to Riff's MIDI IN.\nPlay: you hear the piano and the guitar together.\nTo hear only the guitar, set the keyboard's sound menu to None (MIDI only)."},
ga44(){return"Riff has no keys of its own: the keyboard sends it the notes."},
ga3V(){return"Put the guitar through the amp"},
ga3U(){return"Tap + and pick Amp.\nIn the cable view, drag Riff's AUDIO OUT L to the Amp's AUDIO IN L, then R to R.\nPlay, and turn Drive on the Amp."},
ga3T(){return"The clean guitar gets crunchy or distorted."},
ga3Y(){return"Connect a MIDI controller"},
ga3X(){return"Plug it in over USB (with an OTG adapter on a phone), or switch on a Bluetooth MIDI controller.\nOpen Preferences with the gear icon.\nUnder MIDI Connection, tap Connect MIDI Device and pick it."},
ga3W(){return"It plays the module whose MIDI CH badge matches the channel it sends on, usually 1."},
ga49(){return"Map a knob"},
ga48(){return"Tap the sliders icon at the top of a module.\nTap Learn next to a control, for example Palm mute.\nMove a knob or press a pad on your controller."},
ga47(){return"The control now follows your hardware. The mapping is saved with the project."},
ga40(){return"Start a drum beat"},
ga4_(){return"Tap + and pick Drum Generator.\nPick a pattern from the menu.\nSwitch Active on and press play at the top."},
ga3Z(){return"The beat follows the tempo in the transport bar."},
ga4c(){return"Record a loop"},
ga4b(){return"Tap + and pick Audio Looper.\nIn the cable view, cable the keyboard's AUDIO OUT L and R into the looper's AUDIO IN L and R.\nPress the looper's record button. Recording starts on the first beat of the next bar.\nPlay, then press it again: recording stops at the end of the bar and the loop plays. Press it once more to add a layer."},
ga4a(){return"If the tempo was stopped, it starts and gives you one bar to get ready."},
ga4f(){return"Save and open projects"},
ga4e(){return"Tap the folder icon at the top.\nSave As\u2026 writes your modules, cables and settings to a .gf file.\nNew Project starts over with a keyboard and Xen. Anything not saved is lost.\nOpen Project loads a saved file."},
ga4d(){return"The app also keeps your current session between launches, except in the web demo."},
ga3u(){return"Everything the + button at the bottom of the rack can add. Drag the handle on the left of a module to move it."},
ga4T(){return"Use wired headphones or speakers: Bluetooth adds too much delay to sing live."},
